    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`TokenSequenceMatcher` (`python/sglang/srt/utils/token_sequence_matcher.py`) implements a Knuth-Morris-Pratt (KMP) prefix-table automaton for online token-stream matching.\n\nWhen `advance(matched, token)` is called from the terminal full-match state (`matched == len(self.pattern)`), the failure-link loop immediately indexes `self.pattern[matched]`:\n\n```python\nwhile matched > 0 and token != self.pattern[matched]:\n    matched = self.prefix_lengths[matched - 1]\n```\n\nBecause valid indices of `self.pattern` are `0 .. len(self.pattern) - 1`, calling `advance()` after a full match raises `IndexError: tuple index out of range` instead of transitioning along the KMP failure link `self.prefix_lengths[matched - 1]` to detect subsequent or self-overlapping occurrences in the stream (e.g., pattern `[1, 2, 1]` on stream `[1, 2, 1, 2, 1]`, or single-token pattern `[7]` on `[7, 7]`).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- In `TokenSequenceMatcher.advance()`, transition `matched = self.prefix_lengths[matched - 1]` when `matched == len(self.pattern)` before entering the failure-link loop.\n- Add unit tests in `test/registered/unit/constrained/test_reasoner_grammar_backend.py` (`TestTokenSequenceMatcher`) covering post-match continuation for both self-overlapping multi-token patterns and single-token patterns.\n\n## Credit / Related Work\n\n- `TokenSequenceMatcher` was originally introduced by @JustinTong0323 in #33025 (`[Kimi K3] Add reasoning, tool-call, and OpenAI serving support`).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format Guide](https://docs.sglang.ai/references/contribution_guide.html#format-your-code).\n- [x] Add unit tests as outlined in the [Running and Adding Tests](https://docs.sglang.ai/references/contribution_guide.html#running-and-adding-tests) guide.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41749019611](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/action